            "detectedLanguage": "es",
            "pageCount": 1,
            "processed": true,
            "summary": "This document is an adverse reaction report from Spain concerning a 60-year-old female patient who experienced a serious reaction to Neptazol, a medication taken at a dose of 20 mg orally once a day. The reporting physician is Dr. Fernanda Ruiz. The patient started the medication on July 5, 2026, and discontinued it on July 12, 2026.\n\nOn July 11, 2026, the patient developed a generalized skin rash and fever, which were severe enough to warrant hospitalization for one day. The condition later resolved after treatment. The severity of the adverse reaction is classified as severe based on the need for hospitalization.\n\nThis document is highly relevant for patient safety reviews, as it involves a significant adverse event linked to a medication, indicating possible safety concerns that may need further investigation. The information provided includes details about the medication, the nature of the adverse reaction, and its outcome, making it valuable for assessing the safety profile of Neptazol and monitoring for similar reports.",
            "extractionConfidence": 0.9,
